n with managed OAuth. Search videos, manage playlists, access channel data, and interact with comments. Use this skill when users want to interact with YouTube. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a YouTube connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a YouTube action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with YouTube examples; they add no YouTube capability - YouTube is not an event source, a trigger cannot read YouTube data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":4,"downloads":28930,"installs":885,"stars":145,"versions":14},"createdAt":1770193581120,"updatedAt":1790941264737,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790941138577,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"anotb","slug":"homeassistant-skill","displayName":"Home Assistant Skill","summary":"Inspect and control Home Assistant using REST and supported WebSocket workflows. Discover capabilities, action schemas, device/entity registries, Assist, automations, calendars, energy statistics and diagnostics. Use when the user asks to inspect, troubleshoot or operate an existing Home Assistant installation; not for general smart-home product advice or unrelated device questions.","description":null,"topics":["Rest Api","Smart Home","Weather"],"tags":{"latest":"2.2.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":28492,"installs":264,"stars":16,"versions":6},"createdAt":1770666755697,"updatedAt":1791780955461,"latestVersion":{"version":"2.2.0","createdAt":1791780752913,"changelog":"Add bounded REST/WebSocket readers, registry/Assist/Energy/repair discovery, validation and target queries; correct API examples; document MCP and direct routes; protect credentials and clarify privacy and action effects. 60 tests and Windows/Linux CI.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"HA_URL","required":true},{"key":"HA_TOKEN","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"steipete","slug":"spotify-player","displayName":"Spotify Player","summary":"Terminal Spotify playback/search via spogo (preferred) or spotify_player.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":3,"downloads":28358,"installs":1235,"stars":55,"versions":1},"createdAt":1767545382402,"updatedAt":1779137327234,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545382402,"changelog":"","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"jgarrison929","slug":"security-auditor","displayName":"Security Auditor","summary":"Use when reviewing code for security vulnerabilities, implementing authentication flows, auditing OWASP Top 10, configuring CORS/CSP headers, handling secrets, input validation, SQL injection prevention, XSS protection, or any security-related code review.","description":null,"topics":["Vulnerability","Code Review"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":28235,"installs":871,"stars":47,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770008217892,"updatedAt":1778485987525,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770008217892,"changelog":"Initial release – comprehensive security audit and secure coding skill.\n\n- Provides actionable code review for security vulnerabilities and OWASP Top 10 risks.\n- Includes checklists and code patterns for authentication, CORS/CSP headers, input validation, XSS, SQL injection, secrets handling, and more.\n- Offers recommended secure code snippets and sample security headers.\n- Details best practices for dependency scanning, output formatting, and secure architecture review.\n- Supports structured output for clear, actionable security audit results.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"thesethrose","slug":"marketing-mode","displayName":"Marketing Mode","summary":"Marketing Mode combines 23 comprehensive marketing skills covering strategy, psychology, content, SEO, conversion optimization, and paid growth. Use when users need marketing strategy, copywriting, SEO help, conversion optimization, paid advertising, or any marketing tactic.","description":null,"topics":["Marketing","Knowledge Base"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":7,"downloads":28047,"installs":844,"stars":170,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769016558544,"updatedAt":1778986973131,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769016558544,"changelog":"Complete marketing knowledge base: 23 skills including marketing ideas, psychology, SEO, CRO, paid ads, and launch strategy","license":null},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"microsoft-excel","displayName":"microsoft-excel","summary":"Microsoft Excel API integration with managed OAuth. Read and write Excel workbooks, worksheets, ranges, tables, and charts stored in OneDrive. Use this skill when users want to read or modify Excel spreadsheets, manage worksheet data, work with tables, or access cell values. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Microsoft Excel connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Microsoft Excel action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Microsoft Excel examples; they add no Microsoft Excel capability - Microsoft Excel is not an event source, a trigger cannot read Microsoft Excel data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration","Spreadsheets"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":3,"downloads":27963,"installs":804,"stars":42,"versions":12},"createdAt":1770432008685,"updatedAt":1790939130384,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790939012256,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metada